    rdfs:label "urn:silmaril:entity#instances.papers.07_the_canonical_question.chapters.02_typed_legs_of_the_question.sections.02_quality_and_measurement_legs.concrete_anchor_1#mittenscanonicalquestion" .
silm:instances_papers_07_the_canonical_question_chapters_02_typed_legs_of_the_question_sections_02_quality_and_measurement_legs_concrete_anchor_1#mittenscanonicalquestion silm:hasLongDescription "The MittensCanonicalQuestion is the canonical question of paper 07 posed of the running Mittens fixture: `what answers does this admit?' read as Hom_O(Q_07, -). In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'Q_{07}', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
